The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev);
if (vc4->hang_state)
    vc4_free_hang_state(dev, vc4->hang_state);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the `vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev)` function is called before the `vc4_free_hang_state(dev, vc4->hang_state)` function, which means that if there are still allocated buffer objects (BOs) in the cache when it is being destroyed, it will attempt to free them, leading to errors or crashes.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (vc4->hang_state)
    vc4_free_hang_state(dev, vc4->hang_state);
vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev);
```
Reason:
The fix involves moving the call to `vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev)` after the call to `vc4_free_hang_state(dev, vc4->hang_state)`. This ensures that the hang state is properly freed before the BO cache is destroyed, preventing any attempts to free still-allocated BOs and thus avoiding the errors or crashes associated with the original bug.

